00:37:39.810 --> 00:37:42.450
Can the [INAUDIBLE]
token be copied and used

00:37:42.450 --> 00:37:43.660
in replay attacks?

00:37:43.660 --> 00:37:48.150
Does the IoT mode require RTC
to provide a timestamp element?

00:37:48.150 --> 00:37:50.950
NICOLAS SHIELI: So you don't
need an RTC, but you need time.

00:37:50.950 --> 00:37:51.450
Yes.

00:37:51.450 --> 00:37:54.720
So the job token is valued
for some amount of time,

00:37:54.720 --> 00:37:56.890
and you need to have
time at this point.

00:37:56.890 --> 00:38:01.440
So you're going to get time
from [INAUDIBLE],, for instance.

00:38:01.440 --> 00:38:03.915
So the job token,
when it's signed,

00:38:03.915 --> 00:38:07.320
has a creation date
and an expiration date.

00:38:07.320 --> 00:38:11.010
And on the Google
Cloud Platform site,

00:38:11.010 --> 00:38:15.300
it will be accepting tokens
that are within that time frame.

00:38:15.300 --> 00:38:16.426
It is a policy based thing.

00:38:16.426 --> 00:38:17.383
ANTONY PASSEMARD: Yeah.

00:38:17.383 --> 00:38:19.560
So to clarify-- so when
you create your job,

00:38:19.560 --> 00:38:20.861
you can specify an expiration.

00:38:20.861 --> 00:38:21.860
NICOLAS SHIELI: Correct.

00:38:21.860 --> 00:38:22.410
ANTONY PASSEMARD:
So first, you can

00:38:22.410 --> 00:38:25.800
say my job will be only valued
for 20 minutes, or 10 minutes,

00:38:25.800 --> 00:38:27.660
or whatever.

00:38:27.660 --> 00:38:29.622
The upper bound of
that is 24 hours,

00:38:29.622 --> 00:38:30.830
and there's a little bit of--

00:38:30.830 --> 00:38:34.260
I think there's a few-minute
lag window around that.

00:38:34.260 --> 00:38:38.070
So no more than 24 hours, but
if you specify in your job

00:38:38.070 --> 00:38:41.580
that it's a 20-minute,
30-minute, two-hour validity,

00:38:41.580 --> 00:38:45.275
then this is what the job
can be used for in terms

00:38:45.275 --> 00:38:45.900
of [INAUDIBLE].

00:38:45.900 --> 00:38:48.115
But remember, you need
to sign that [INAUDIBLE]

00:38:48.115 --> 00:38:49.240
with a private [INAUDIBLE].

00:38:49.240 --> 00:38:50.864
It's not only copying
the [INAUDIBLE],,

00:38:50.864 --> 00:38:53.310
you need to have access to
the private key to sign it,

00:38:53.310 --> 00:38:55.165
otherwise you won't be able
to use that [INAUDIBLE]..

00:38:55.165 --> 00:38:55.470
NICOLAS SHIELI: Right.

00:38:55.470 --> 00:38:57.360
So you don't need
[INAUDIBLE] hardware,

00:38:57.360 --> 00:38:58.870
because you're
typically connected,

00:38:58.870 --> 00:39:00.590
so you are able to get time.

00:39:04.100 --> 00:39:07.140
ANTONY PASSEMARD: So let me
see other questions here.

00:39:07.140 --> 00:39:10.350
Is it possible to do
firmware device update

00:39:10.350 --> 00:39:15.440
and then update the ATECC608A
with a new hash secure boot?

00:39:15.440 --> 00:39:15.940
Yeah.

00:39:15.940 --> 00:39:18.023
NICOLAS SHIELI: Yes, so
that's an important point.

00:39:18.023 --> 00:39:20.760
So indeed, the 608A
has a few features

00:39:20.760 --> 00:39:23.640
that allow you to handle
this use case of [INAUDIBLE]..

00:39:23.640 --> 00:39:26.910
So basically, the 608A
will, the first time

00:39:26.910 --> 00:39:29.760
you're going to be using
it, will receive the hash

00:39:29.760 --> 00:39:31.790
from the microcontroller
and then will

00:39:31.790 --> 00:39:36.390
receive the signature that was
generated by the private key

00:39:36.390 --> 00:39:38.287
at the time of
signing the firmware.

00:39:38.287 --> 00:39:39.370
It will receive those two.

00:39:39.370 --> 00:39:41.110
It will validate
that they are valid.

00:39:41.110 --> 00:39:43.290
If they are valid, it
will store them both.

00:39:43.290 --> 00:39:43.860
Right?

00:39:43.860 --> 00:39:46.695
Now, if you're coming
up with a new firmware,

00:39:46.695 --> 00:39:47.820
it will be a new signature.

00:39:47.820 --> 00:39:50.606
So you're going to be
passing the new digest

00:39:50.606 --> 00:39:51.480
with a new signature.

00:39:51.480 --> 00:39:56.130
And then the device is able
to, again, be matched, verified

00:39:56.130 --> 00:39:57.712
correctly with the public key.

00:39:57.712 --> 00:39:59.670
We'll update its content
with the new signature

00:39:59.670 --> 00:40:00.779
and a new digest.

