00:44:53.070 --> 00:44:57.780
Is IoT Core IaaS or PaaS, and
how would you describe it?

00:44:57.780 --> 00:44:59.820
So IoT Core is a
fully managed service.

00:44:59.820 --> 00:45:01.590
It's not an
infrastructured service.

00:45:01.590 --> 00:45:04.370
It's almost [INAUDIBLE]
if you think about it.

00:45:04.370 --> 00:45:05.250
It's an endpoint.

00:45:05.250 --> 00:45:07.230
So when you log into
your cd console,

00:45:07.230 --> 00:45:08.970
you'll see at the
bottom left, there's

00:45:08.970 --> 00:45:10.549
going to be a link
called IoT Core.

00:45:10.549 --> 00:45:11.340
You'll go in there.

00:45:11.340 --> 00:45:13.332
The first thing you do
is you create a registry

00:45:13.332 --> 00:45:14.290
and you give it a name.

00:45:14.290 --> 00:45:16.590
And inside that
registry, create a device

00:45:16.590 --> 00:45:18.330
and upload your public key.

00:45:18.330 --> 00:45:19.740
That's all you have to do.

00:45:19.740 --> 00:45:21.190
And that's it.

00:45:21.190 --> 00:45:22.730
There's no
configuration, nothing.

00:45:22.730 --> 00:45:25.274
Then you have
mqtt.googleapi.com,

00:45:25.274 --> 00:45:26.190
that's your end point.

00:45:26.190 --> 00:45:27.550
As I said, it's a
global endpoint.

00:45:27.550 --> 00:45:28.650
You don't have to
think about where you.

00:45:28.650 --> 00:45:30.233
You don't have to
think about the fact

00:45:30.233 --> 00:45:33.570
that you're in Australia, in
the US, in Europe, in Japan.

00:45:33.570 --> 00:45:34.890
Doesn't matter.

00:45:34.890 --> 00:45:37.680
We'll [INAUDIBLE] to the
closest Google Front End

00:45:37.680 --> 00:45:40.726
and get that traffic to the
region where you want it to be.

00:45:40.726 --> 00:45:42.350
So there's one region
globally that you

00:45:42.350 --> 00:45:46.080
use to have your Device Manager,
but the connectivity is global.

00:45:46.080 --> 00:45:49.290
The data lands into
the region you choose.

00:45:49.290 --> 00:45:51.210
So a fully, fully
managed service.

00:45:51.210 --> 00:45:53.570
No load balancing
policy, nothing.

00:45:53.570 --> 00:45:58.260
No scaling policy, no cluster,
no shards, none of that.

00:45:58.260 --> 00:45:59.340
No VM, nothing.

00:45:59.340 --> 00:46:00.706
No updates.

00:46:00.706 --> 00:46:01.830
Everything is done for you.

00:46:01.830 --> 00:46:04.880
It's a fully managed service.

00:46:04.880 --> 00:46:07.805
How Cloud IoT Core help the
global corporation to scale,

00:46:07.805 --> 00:46:10.310
as the number of
IoT-connected devices

00:46:10.310 --> 00:46:13.040
can vary tremendously
across the globe?

00:46:13.040 --> 00:46:16.210
I believe that's one
of our core strengths.

00:46:16.210 --> 00:46:17.084
There's two things.

00:46:17.084 --> 00:46:18.750
First, it's a managed
service by Google.

00:46:18.750 --> 00:46:21.570
So we will manage the
scaling up and down for you.

00:46:21.570 --> 00:46:23.129
You don't have to
think about it.

00:46:23.129 --> 00:46:25.420
You can send us 10 million
devices, 20 million devices.

00:46:25.420 --> 00:46:27.715
It doesn't really matter to us.

00:46:27.715 --> 00:46:29.090
You don't have to
think about it.

00:46:29.090 --> 00:46:30.650
That's our job to do.

00:46:30.650 --> 00:46:33.080
And Google does that
really well, as you know.

00:46:33.080 --> 00:46:36.320
Just look at YouTube and Gmail
and all those other services,

00:46:36.320 --> 00:46:39.980
and search, and ad distribution,
all of that are superscaled,

00:46:39.980 --> 00:46:42.590
and that's what we
use to power IoT Core.

00:46:42.590 --> 00:46:45.080
The other thing is you're
talking about global scale.

00:46:45.080 --> 00:46:47.090
The cool thing about the
global network we have

00:46:47.090 --> 00:46:49.850
is because when you
use mqtt.googleapi.com,

00:46:49.850 --> 00:46:51.530
it is globally distributed.

00:46:51.530 --> 00:46:55.580
If you have a network of devices
that is globally distributed,

00:46:55.580 --> 00:46:58.100
you will actually
automatically load balance

00:46:58.100 --> 00:47:00.740
across the
hundred-plus Front End

00:47:00.740 --> 00:47:02.070
that we have across the globe.

00:47:02.070 --> 00:47:05.750
So you're not hitting the same
Front End by all your millions

00:47:05.750 --> 00:47:07.250
of devices across the globe.

00:47:07.250 --> 00:47:09.380
They will be
automatically distributed,

00:47:09.380 --> 00:47:13.010
which helps a lot with
the distribution of upload

00:47:13.010 --> 00:47:13.740
across the globe.

00:47:13.740 --> 00:47:16.850
So we're really well
architected to do exactly

00:47:16.850 --> 00:47:21.760
that, the big global
corporation ad scale.

